{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"a65c9efd-ca71-4efe-92f0-d22578134402","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have updated the prompt caching configuration and documented the changes in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-kGqwAV/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n- **Modified [`build_system`](file:///tmp/h-kGqwAV/bot.py#L130-L137) in [bot.py](file:///tmp/h-kGqwAV/bot.py)**:\n  - Previously, `INSTRUCTIONS` and `athlete_context` were concatenated into a single text block with one `cache_control` marker, causing any memory updates via `save_fact` to invalidate the cache for the entire system prompt.\n  - Split the `system` parameter into two distinct blocks with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`:\n    1. The byte-stable, static instructions (`INSTRUCTIONS`).\n    2. The volatile per-athlete context (`athlete_context(a, today)`), containing profile, date, and long-term memory facts.\n- **Wrote [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-kGqwAV/ANSWER.md)** explaining the problem, the changes made, and their effect on caching behavior.\n","duration_seconds":53.223795,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":110230,"output_tokens":1595,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":204081,"total_tokens":111825}}}
